#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059848 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059453 :question/id #uuid "d7516cec-bd96-59db-98cd-5d82e41fa719" :question/math-academy-id "e-14763" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $A$ given below?\n\n- $\\det(A) = 0$\n\n- $A$ is **not** a singular matrix\n\n- $A$ is a singular matrix\n\n![](images/21/21cd71e00c682ad1117b9ae126adcbeb8e4c55769c73eae1e1169534f2a01d4a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(0-4)-2(7-3)+3(4-0) \\\\  & =-4-2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-4-8+12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049125 :topic/math-academy-id 863 :topic/title "Introduction to the Inverse of a Matrix"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc68d302-4e05-53f4-a13b-62357c5a7653" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439477} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd87d1e-fd23-5dab-bc43-900e69f9433c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc68d302-4e05-53f4-a13b-62357c5a7653" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439477} :answer-field/id #uuid "91107b81-23d7-5b15-b57e-bf4ab1565fe8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440096} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70ca64ce-81b4-5636-ba58-791451017b65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439479} {:answer/id #uuid "e05c2887-d7f6-57d2-a4c2-2f2da18a616f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70ca64ce-81b4-5636-ba58-791451017b65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439479} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2548bbb-9529-57ff-80c9-7eb2135baee7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440097} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b319f9de-b31e-5b7f-b008-19047e4bc681" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439481} {:answer/id #uuid "7743ec0d-8e7c-52c8-b5bf-a2c3ff1639ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7743ec0d-8e7c-52c8-b5bf-a2c3ff1639ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439482} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3fd9d3c-6b34-5cd5-b3aa-e7329f24b386" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440098}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0d9bc49-c94e-5174-9068-2abf75c42684" :question/math-academy-id "q-128490" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $M$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $det(M)=10$\n- **II.** $det(M)=-5$\n- **III.** $M$ is a singular matrix\n\n \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 4\\end{aligned}|+\\frac{1}{3}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}(12-15)-0+\\frac{1}{3}(0+9\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\cdot (-3)+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{5}+3\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(M)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060454 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "141d3bda-708e-5cd1-a9c3-33813075f0e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438670} {:answer/id #uuid "c97bfd73-22d0-514a-b96a-af8b07567307" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c97bfd73-22d0-514a-b96a-af8b07567307" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438671} :answer-field/id #uuid "e441ef7a-f7d8-556c-897f-7d0c7a6b2bc1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa853019-8cb7-57bb-8d89-07bb087c8654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438672} {:answer/id #uuid "5e56b566-9992-53f1-aacf-331d0f084061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e56b566-9992-53f1-aacf-331d0f084061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438673} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6cc4081-efb3-5cbd-91d9-77bb4d9690f4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439365} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1db0c840-997f-55b7-bab1-3572f80549a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438674} {:answer/id #uuid "9da77c68-30c2-574d-8a12-c8183bf926de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1db0c840-997f-55b7-bab1-3572f80549a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438674} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e1cd461-5747-5d77-9466-83683a668421" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439366}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4279505-241a-54e3-b9b3-ff9b46d09cfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-9838" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $F$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $det(F)=0$\n- **II.** $F$ is a singular matrix\n- **III.** $det(F)=-2$\n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(F) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-1(24-30)+2(21-24) \\\\  & =0-1\\cdot (-6)+2\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =6-6 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(F)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262906 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "938435d8-69e4-5177-83be-c2661b220df3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437788} {:answer/id #uuid "b0acf52f-1926-563b-90fe-5bd5c838a2cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "938435d8-69e4-5177-83be-c2661b220df3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437788} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef069a99-e51d-5c41-b3dd-fbe618b3ae29" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438923} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fda1810e-40d9-5b5a-8ed9-7de0e91b6696" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437790} {:answer/id #uuid "ae8badb5-ccf3-54b7-bf14-15f19c3c783e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fda1810e-40d9-5b5a-8ed9-7de0e91b6696" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437790} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a6baa2c-bfa2-5841-829c-446168fc4d31" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438924} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd3030ea-f56b-54f2-b19e-0fe96063ba8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437792} {:answer/id #uuid "13768b60-6037-5979-87a7-85e46aa637f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd3030ea-f56b-54f2-b19e-0fe96063ba8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437792} :answer-field/id #uuid "10609156-1bc3-5176-82f7-7da72d8cac5c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438925}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f86fe2f1-042a-5183-8a18-518a658cc1a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-128474" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $Q$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $det(Q)=-5$\n- **II.** $det(Q)=1$\n- **III.** $Q$ is **not** a singular matrix\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(9-5)-1(6-3)-1(10-9) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4-3-1 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(Q)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, none of the statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262908 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9c8a655-dc30-5747-b5e0-efd4fa464943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437794} {:answer/id #uuid "b3238a25-1600-54c9-a92e-d6b1f31166ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9c8a655-dc30-5747-b5e0-efd4fa464943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437794} :answer-field/id #uuid "0457a549-1799-5124-a11e-6cbe8bf02f40" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438926} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86770289-d595-5a74-8241-7f7eaf943501" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437796} {:answer/id #uuid "0065df67-0fde-5ae4-ab1b-04075255afaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0065df67-0fde-5ae4-ab1b-04075255afaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437797} :answer-field/id #uuid "48c446f0-c232-5d1a-a9fa-08c4d973bbe4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438927} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06d221ff-7342-5189-8083-2e45e2305d69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437798} {:answer/id #uuid "db168e14-a68a-5486-95d1-8d4686854e72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db168e14-a68a-5486-95d1-8d4686854e72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437799} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b5f6d45-4846-5d6c-b409-f20f073263eb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438928}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "898815e0-65a8-55f9-b81f-a64efbb5e7e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-128476" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $T$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $T$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $T$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- **III.** $det(T)=-30$\n\n \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1-3)-3(2-1)-5(6-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-2-3-25 \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(T)=-30\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96a78a3a-a96f-5296-bb6f-17bd0c2c1029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437812} {:answer/id #uuid "8a41bcde-2807-5a96-8245-df7493039a41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a41bcde-2807-5a96-8245-df7493039a41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437813} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d87a851-8d26-5425-83e8-dba94be07b21" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438935} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d06dd62-d83d-54e9-b4ea-1974429d75ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437814} {:answer/id #uuid "423c9da1-fb5c-5eb1-aac0-e8f7d5033fa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "423c9da1-fb5c-5eb1-aac0-e8f7d5033fa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437815} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad0097cd-c1c7-5438-b4af-b5844d0cf50a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438936} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e2b6e65-193a-5e1a-ae4e-babcf8cd0b3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437816} {:answer/id #uuid "4daf1704-b4bb-5190-aede-54368b9e49c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e2b6e65-193a-5e1a-ae4e-babcf8cd0b3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437816} :answer-field/id #uuid "727b8a81-c497-5e39-8d74-82d5d2b34ab9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438937}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0d8a3d8-8c1e-55f4-b495-022734d0f802" :question/math-academy-id "q-128484" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $R$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $R$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $det(R)=0$\n- **III.** $det(R)=1$\n\n \n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{aligned}|-\\sqrt{2}|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(0+\\sqrt{2})-\\sqrt{2}(2+1)+2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 3+2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}-3\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(R)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326671 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6ffe837-0ba9-566a-847f-01c50e5b0d4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438254} {:answer/id #uuid "0c851c6e-8e6f-5ce1-85f0-794bba8508bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c851c6e-8e6f-5ce1-85f0-794bba8508bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438255} :answer-field/id #uuid "ece7019d-4e4a-54c5-8c4b-3ee796bd1176" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439156} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69b3cb09-83cc-54f2-9f3a-46d5234e0bc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438256} {:answer/id #uuid "e013cbff-c909-515f-a71d-027cdb4811c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69b3cb09-83cc-54f2-9f3a-46d5234e0bc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438256} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bcb1241-521a-5c92-ac65-6398206509ea" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439157} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1785546f-b00e-5a43-be50-0c26a6fc2ca6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438258} {:answer/id #uuid "1c201000-e71f-5609-9f1d-19bba5ab4630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1785546f-b00e-5a43-be50-0c26a6fc2ca6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438258} :answer-field/id #uuid "e28dc200-2ac1-54de-90ea-6e018bd1ba08" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439158}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "084b3fe8-adf9-5ab7-9017-b2d4d829ca62" :question/math-academy-id "q-38179" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $E$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $E$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $E$ is **not**  a singular matrix\n- **III.** $det(E)=-2$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 5 & 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(E) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 5 & 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 8\\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 5 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(40-42)-3(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{12}{3})+4(\\frac{14}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}+4\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{12}{3}+\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(E)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326673 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79e4e142-7005-54c1-8d51-b38fccf87ef4" :answer/ty