on.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f2a72ef8-dad7-5172-8868-8d2781696df8" :question/math-academy-id "q-38182" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $Q$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $Q$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- **II.** $Q$ is a singular matrix\n- **III.** $det(Q)=-5$\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-3(8-14)+6(5-8) \\\\  & =0-3\\cdot (-6)+6\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =18-18 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(Q)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89dca9db-88dc-5f58-9f23-ec98ca1bbc75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438478} {:answer/id #uuid "128f9548-3706-5b6d-94e4-afd0ea31e354" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "128f9548-3706-5b6d-94e4-afd0ea31e354" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438479} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8abcdf3-f784-54de-90bb-b51f314f8912" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439268} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b74bddc-ad74-5f61-a0ce-c1bb3f545d9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/t