alue "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261005} {:answer/id #uuid "8c6b36bf-bffd-5918-ae53-d958ad6e391a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81ca9339-6bce-5219-8fae-787545463a11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261005} :answer-field/id #uuid "c45caafc-858f-500e-9ef9-058205b847f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262475}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb6a7e0a-d356-5b58-a703-e0864f9a1a58" :question/math-academy-id "q-128500" :question/problem "Given that\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ y & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand $det(B)=12,$ find the value of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(B) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ y & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ y & 1\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ y & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2\\cdot (1-y)-5\\cdot (2-2y) \\\\  & =12y-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $12,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12y-12 & =12 \\\\ 12y & =24 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "183c086d-012b-5f39-b92e-4550955dfcbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260085} {:answer/id #uuid "2044861f-98f6-51d9-9cf5-e5080be450a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260152} {:answer/id #uuid "21a46985-36f6-5f1d-b213-16f3935ec5b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260165} {:answer/id #uuid "91c5f6e6-19cd-5455-92f6-06f29a9d6687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261142} {:answer/id #uuid "c0800f44-af37-5d5d-b586-92ebc2148392" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0800f44-af37-5d5d-b586-92ebc2148392" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261575} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a39ba2f-181c-558b-b3c6-6fdf22cdca96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262399}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9517ddd6-18dd-5bea-948b-a75416c96cbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-128502" :question/problem "Given that \n$C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & q & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ \nand $det(C)=28,$ find the value of $q.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & q & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}q & 5 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}-1 & q \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (q+25)-3\\cdot (-1)+5 \\\\  & =2q+58\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $28,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2q+58 & =28 \\\\ 2q & =-30 \\\\ q & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a96a6f2b-900e-5634-9638-19c6ba6bffea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439527} {:answer/id #uuid "5d1afda0-1dac-5620-821a-ad4de506b094" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a96a6f2b-900e-5634-9638-19