r/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439553} {:answer/id #uuid "a410470b-bb5c-5e99-9ef1-c4f15f64a1e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7f79edc-2997-5309-a8e1-d7e987ae7695" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439553} :answer-field/id #uuid "d21ddfff-201d-565d-875a-ebc1c438bce9" :answer-field/key "VIII" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440134}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c642acf-da11-5fe2-a467-6e32aaff486e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130580" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of\n$[\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 3 \\\\ 5 & x & 7 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nis $22$, find all the possible values of $x.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $x=-8$\n- **II.** $x=-5$\n- **III.** $x=-3$\n- **IV.** $x=-1$\n- **V.** $x=3$\n- **VI.** $x=5$\n- **VII.** $x=7$\n- **VIII.** $x=8$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 3 \\\\ 5 & x & 7 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =x|\\begin{aligned}x & 7 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2x|\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}5 & x \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x(x-14)-2x(5-21)+3(10-3x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-14x+32x+30-9x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+9x+30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $22,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+9x+30 & =22 \\\\ {x}^{2}+9x+8 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{-9\\pm \\sqrt{{9}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 8}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9\\pm 7}{2} \\\\  & =-8,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-8$ and $x=-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265943 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08612547-b005-5392-af1a-df7b474c183f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263076} {:answer/id #uuid "44c75865-eba7-5ea5-899b-6ea970d46b60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263604} {:answer/id #uuid "540dadca-dfc9-5c4a-a4a7-eb33cde6b83b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263725} {:answer/id #uuid "73317ca7-7b96-518c-af47-8c1a296a0e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263999} {:answer/id #uuid "fc9e8555-066d-500b-b643-2c20d52ada5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08612547-b005-5392-af1a-df7b474c183f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263076} :answer-field/id #uuid "f52b9c18-1a55-5825-8634-6431340dd06d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265685}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7e9e0a1f-e62f-537b-9ae4-39884aaf945c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130620" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $x$ given that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ x & -1 & -x\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ x & -1 & -x\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -x\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ x & -x\\end{aligned}|+8|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ x & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(-x+2)-5(-x-2x)+8(-1-x) \\\\  & =-3x+6+15x-8-8x \\\\  & =4x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265945 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21390a7b-0a54-5e9a-9011-c7deff139c41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{5}{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263297} {:answer/id #uuid "91d75f72-1a96-5644-a529-caf7355ab1bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Any value of $p$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264249} {:answer/id #uuid "970c8319-2067-5d80-a590-021621a09030" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-3$ and $3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264292} {:answer/id #uuid "f080186a-d1c4-58fa-9d1f-db014dd38fcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265109} {:answer/id #uuid "fc1c675c-a294-5ee2-a8ca-549d874e48c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-10$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91d75f72-1a96-5644-a529-caf7355ab1bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Any value of $p$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264249} :answer-field/id #uuid "a69f31fe-6848-54a7-8e0e-0e1258ee7ad2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265543}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fee93468-4926-51f6-9486-b49c687c7f2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130626" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $p$ given that the matrix\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3p & 4 \\\\ -2 & 6p & -8 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3p & 4 \\\\ -2 & 6p & -8 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}6p & -8 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-3p)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6p \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(6p-8)+3p(-2+8)+4(2-6p) \\\\  & =6p-8+18p+8-24p \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, this matrix is singular for all values of $p.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21022c7d-b6d6-5cae-a0a4-a57d89afab0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285086} {:answer/id #uuid "49921218-a78e-55ed-9401-67d5dff3f875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285465} {:answer/id #uuid "5f92b6ee-a669-5379-82fa-e12d81b14834" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285665} {:answer/id #uuid "62d465ea-c086-5e0e-baf0-37c50f53cd7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285692} {:answer/id #uuid "b073025c-0c72-5876-88dd-01988080f163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49921218-a78e-55ed-9401-67d5dff3f875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285465} :answer-field/id #uuid "43436436-3068-54a8-97bc-a4c069c2a82c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287296}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa24bddc-180c-5ff0-88bc-f05ee3a66fe1" :question/math-academy-id "q-18252" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $p$ given that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -5 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -5 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2p-4+10)-0+(-10-6) \\\\  & =2p-4+10-10-6 \\\\  & =2p-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0.$ So,  we have:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2p-10 & =0 \\\\ 2p & =10 \\\\ p & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $p=5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "458cafbf-7052-5688-a3e6-270feaa693c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439555} {:answer/id #uuid "f155cb5b-192c-558c-aa25-73d859f68f54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439556}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f155cb5b-192c-558c-aa25-73d859f68f54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439556} :answer-field/id #uuid "11461a6e-1dea-5d60-87fb-79ffe64218c2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440135} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac822410-bfae-5d59-9738-427934044f97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439557} {:answer/id #uuid "0258f679-5bbb-5a4f-8ebb-3d4abeaeab7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac822410-bfae-5d59-9738-427934044f97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439557} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1d050ea-e9d9-5e3c-ba92-d504ed6a5ce7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440136} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fee28db-a2fa-5c8a-b01b-25dceb5db556" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value 